{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 956 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8704150e4e7efc2cc43aca60763c87c9a5f762396ae3c56a9f972a44327bd9c2" :edb/db-before-t 955 :edb/db-after-t 956 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534268 50 #inst "2026-10-06T15:24:10.308Z" 13194139534268 true] [17592186083207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283090 13194139534268 true] [17592186083207 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283097 13194139534268 true] [17592186083240 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283078 13194139534268 true] [17592186083247 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283071 13194139534268 true] [17592186083247 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283085 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283072 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1089 "q-127390" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ If the critical points of $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi )$ are $x={x}_{1}$ and $x={x}_{2},$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1113 #uuid "c236be5c-f7ce-577e-8440-1e61c10bf0dc" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283071 1145 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})+n\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi <x<\\pi .$\n\n- setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$\n\n- setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi <x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions to this equation for $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi )$ are \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\,x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi )$ are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283073 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283074 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283075 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283076 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283077 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1041 "selection" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283077 13194139534268 true] [17592186283072 1110 #uuid "65add198-edef-57ec-9f82-e394376b4295" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283073 1034 "-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283073 1111 #uuid "5b1d1a2e-5cdf-5c6a-ace8-818954c38398" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283074 1034 "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283074 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283074 1111 #uuid "4d92fd6d-c367-5859-8da2-c1a317efa08a" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283075 1034 "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283075 1111 #uuid "ef2def8a-cf94-57a8-997e-089a9c22b797" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283076 1034 "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283076 1111 #uuid "78a9a3dd-c88a-5730-8af8-49e3e561841a" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283077 1034 "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283077 1111 #uuid "b84874f0-d9f9-5284-b498-0d91ad0d6cea" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283079 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1089 "q-132464" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1100 "What are the critical points of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+6}?$" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1113 #uuid "020c0b00-cb4a-56fb-b3c8-84c40dc80072" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283078 1145 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)^{′}\\cdot ({x}^{2}+6)-(x-2)\\cdot ({x}^{2}+6)^{′}}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+6)-(x-2)\\cdot 2x}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+6-2{x}^{2}+4x}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+4x+6}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x-6}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x$ by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x-6}{({x}^{2}+6)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x-6 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-4-6 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=2\\pm \\sqrt{10}.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=2\\pm \\sqrt{10}.$" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283080 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283081 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283082 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283083 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283084 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1041 "selection" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283084 13194139534268 true] [17592186283079 1110 #uuid "bf076dfe-9ae6-539c-81af-8a6891189af3" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283080 1034 "x=-2\\pm \\sqrt{10}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283080 1111 #uuid "4039e1a7-cc37-51a3-ab37-2c71b8952690" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283081 1034 "x=2\\pm \\sqrt{2}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283081 1111 #uuid "8630c70d-ec2e-5494-9ac9-e24c2e41a159" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283082 1034 "x=2\\pm \\sqrt{5}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534268 true] [17592186283082 1111 #uuid "f3695305-1cab-5741-bf86-c34271fd5d71" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283083 1034 "x=-2\\pm \\sqrt{6}" 13194139534268 true] [17592186283083 1103 #edb/